//- SETTINGS - MANIFEST-DRIVEN CONFIG FORM ON THE HOUSE +field MIXIN, SO
//- SENSITIVE KEEP-ON-BLANK + __clear COME FOR FREE. SAVES AUTO-FIRE ON
//- CHANGE (HOUSE FORM CONVENTION); THE RESPONSE RE-RENDERS THIS SURFACE
//- AND DROPS THE TOAST IN THE TAKEOVER HEADER. LAYOUT = .appSettingsGroup
//- ROWS (TITLE+BLURB RAIL | CARD) - SEE apps.css SETTINGS BLOCK.
//- sectionData: { configured, formFields [+field DESCRIPTORS + key],
//-               showDefault, contentTypeLabels }
include ../../../mixins/field

include ../sectionTitleDivider

if !sectionData.configured
  .appSettingsWelcome
    .welcomeTitle Welcome to #{activeApp.display_name}!
    .welcomeSubtitle Let's get it connected - fill in the fields below and the rail dot goes green.

.appSettingsGroup
  .appSettingsGroupInfo
    .request-section-header Connection
    .appSettingsGroupBlurb Where #{activeApp.display_name} lives and how DiscoFlix signs in. Changes save as you make them.
  .appSettingsGroupBody
    form.appSettingsForm(
      hx-post=`/apps/${activeApp.id}/save`
      hx-trigger="change, submit"
      hx-swap="none"
    )
      .appFormCard
        .appSettingsFields
          each f in sectionData.formFields
            +field(f, f.key, activeApp.id, false)
    .appSectionActions
      button.modal-button.button-secondary(
        hx-post=`/apps/${activeApp.id}/test`
        hx-target="#appTestResult"
        hx-swap="outerHTML"
      ) Test Connection
      span#appTestResult

if sectionData.showDefault
  .appSettingsGroup
    .appSettingsGroupInfo
      .request-section-header Request Routing
      .appSettingsGroupBlurb Which instance catches new #{sectionData.contentTypeLabels.join(' and ')} requests when more than one could serve them.
    .appSettingsGroupBody
      .appDefaultRow
        if activeApp.is_default
          span.appDefaultChip Default
          span.appDefaultText New #{sectionData.contentTypeLabels.join(' and ')} requests land here unless an admin picks another instance.
        else
          span.appDefaultText Another instance currently takes new #{sectionData.contentTypeLabels.join(' and ')} requests.
          button.modal-button.button-secondary(
            hx-post=`/apps/${activeApp.id}/default`
            hx-swap="none"
          ) Make Default

.appSettingsGroup
  .appSettingsGroupInfo
    .request-section-header.danger Danger Zone
    .appSettingsGroupBlurb Disconnect #{activeApp.display_name} from DiscoFlix.
  .appSettingsGroupBody
    .appDangerZone
      .appDangerZoneText
        | Removing #[strong #{activeApp.display_name}] deletes its connection settings from DiscoFlix. The service itself isn't touched, and past requests keep their history.
      button.appRemoveButton(
        hx-get=`/modal/apps/remove/${activeApp.id}`
        hx-target="#modals-here"
        hx-trigger="click"
        data-bs-toggle="modal"
        data-bs-target="#modals-here"
      ) Remove App
